  "articleBody": "A wobbly stair handrail isn't just annoying; it can be a real safety hazard. Often, the culprit is pretty simple: either the mounting brackets aren't secured properly, or they're not anchored into solid framing. Many DIYers miss the studs or joists when installing, leading to anchors that can't hold up to daily use. Another common issue is having the brackets spaced too far apart, which lets the rail flex and feel unstable. If you’re using hollow wall anchors instead of screwing directly into studs, especially on a heavily used staircase, you’re likely to run into wobbling pretty quickly. Consistent height is also crucial – an uneven rail can feel loose even if it's securely fastened in places. Make sure to check if your brackets are loose, or if the fasteners themselves have stripped out. Sometimes, it’s a matter of the rail material itself not being rigid enough for the span between brackets. If you're encountering persistent wobbles, or if your stairway is complex, it's a good idea to bring in a professional. They can quickly diagnose the problem and ensure your handrail is safe and sturdy for years to come. Don't risk a fall!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
